// Ground truth. Hand-written — this is the point.
//
// If a model writes these questions and a model judges the answers, the
// ablation table measures a model's agreement with itself and nothing else.
// Sixty questions is a few evenings of work and it is what makes every other
// number in this repository mean something.
//
// Format, one JSON object per line:
//   question         what a researcher would actually type
//   relevant_chunks  chunk ids that genuinely support an answer, found by
//                    reading — not by running retrieval and accepting the top
//                    hits, which would label the system correct by definition
//   answer_facts     short strings that a correct answer must contain; used by
//                    the Phase III faithfulness check, ignored before then
//   kind             lookup | comparison | synthesis | absent
//   note             why this question is here, for whoever re-labels later
//
// "absent" questions matter as much as the rest: a question the corpus cannot
// answer, where the correct behaviour is to decline. Without them the system is
// never scored on refusal, and refusal is a prediction.
//
// The _meta row records the chunking parameters these ids were written under.
// The harness refuses to score if the chunker has changed since.
{"_meta": true, "chunking": "c1000-o180", "labelled_by": "hand", "labelled_on": "2026-08-31"}
